Equation (12-46) implies that the Eotvos number cannot exceed a value of about 16. Since the spherical-cap regime requires Eo $ \geq $ 40(see Fig. 2.5), stability considerations explain why drops falling in gases and drops in many liquid systems never attain the spherical-cap regime. Moreover, since We = $ 4\mathrm{Eo}/3 C_{\mathrm{D}} $ and $ C_{\mathrm{D}} $ is nearly constant for large drops in air, it is also possible to

